    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3845\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to office-based\nsurgery\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThis bill makes a technical correction to Chapter 365 of the Laws of\n2007 regarding the oversight of office-based surgery.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection one amends paragraph (i) of subdivision 1 of section 230-d of\nthe public Health Law by adding language to the definition of,\n\"Licensee\" stipulating that it does not include an individual licensed\nunder both Articles 131 and 133 of the Education Law who is practicing\nin a professional service corporation, or any other entity authorized\nonly to engage in the practice of dentistry.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\nNone.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nChapter 365 of the Laws of 2007 enacted provisions, recommended by the\nDepartment of Health, regarding the oversight of office-based surgery.\nThe intent of the measure was to provide oversight of physicians who\nperform surgical procedures in a location other than a hospital.\nDentists were not intended to be included under this new statute.\nHowever, because some dentists are licensed physicians, the law has\nunintentionally brought their practices under the office-based surgery\noversight provisions. This is a technical amendment that will correct\nthat situation.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone\n\n LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
